IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Carbon Pricing Act 2018 (Singapore) -- registration of a business facility and of the person who controls it (ss 3, 4, 7, 8,
-- 9(1)-(3)), emissions reports and their verification (ss 11, 12), the carbon tax and allowances (ss 16, 20C; Third Schedule
-- Part 1), paying the tax with fixed-price carbon credits and the late-payment penalties (s 17; Third Schedule Part 2), the
-- appeal to the Minister (s 34(1), (2)), and the offences the operator of a facility can commit (ss 54-59, 62(1)).
--
-- SEAT: the person who has operational control of a business facility -- the operator who must register, report and pay.
-- Every decision is phrased as that person would ask it.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 1/1/2024; SSO "Current version as at 01 Oct
-- 2026"), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CPA2018.txt, with Act 37 of 2022 (wef 1 January 2024) shown.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the Agency's administration and powers (ss 6, 46-51), s 13 monitoring plans beyond their place in s 12, the
-- Agency's directions (s 14), refunds (s 19), recovery (s 20), the Minister's award of allowances (ss 20D-20G: the award is an
-- input), assessments and their revision (ss 21-25) beyond the deadline they set, the credits registry (ss 26-33D) beyond the
-- carbon price, appeal procedure (ss 35-39), registers (ss 41-44), the evidence and service provisions (Part 9), offences by
-- officers and other persons (ss 60, 61), composition (s 71) and regulations (s 76). The industry sectors to which the Act
-- applies are prescribed by regulations (s 5(1)) that were not deposited: every rule here assumes the operator's sector is one.
-- Part 2 of the Second Schedule (non-reckonable emissions) is not transcribed: the operator states those amounts as facts.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the individual
-- to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test
-- pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Carbon Pricing Act 2018 -- the operator of a business facility`

§§ `Second Schedule Part 1 -- emissions thresholds`

-- Second Schedule, Part 1: "1. The first emissions threshold is 2,000 tCO2e." "2. The second emissions threshold is 25,000
-- tCO2e." (tCO2e: metric tonnes of carbon dioxide equivalence, s 2(1).)
`the first emissions threshold` MEANS 2000
`the second emissions threshold` MEANS 25000

§§ `2 -- reckonable GHG emissions`

-- s 2(1): "reckonable GHG emission" means "any GHG emission other than a non-reckonable GHG emission". A non-reckonable emission
-- is a gas emitted in the circumstances in Part 2 of the Second Schedule; an "excluded GHG emission" is one in Part 3 (vehicles
-- transporting persons or goods; AFOLU activities). The operator states each amount in tCO2e, the three taken as not overlapping.
GIVEN `my GHG emissions` IS A NUMBER
      `of which non-reckonable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `my reckonable emissions` IS `my GHG emissions` MINUS `of which non-reckonable`

-- s 11(2): the emissions report sets out the GHG emissions "(other than excluded GHG emissions)"; s 16(1A): the total on which
-- tax is charged is "as set out in the emissions report". INFERENCE (not stated in the text): excluded emissions are reckonable
-- by the s 2 definition, so they count towards the s 7 thresholds, but they are not in the report, so they are not taxed.
GIVEN `my GHG emissions` IS A NUMBER
      `of which non-reckonable` IS A NUMBER
      `of which excluded` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `my reckonable emissions as reported` IS
    `my reckonable emissions` `my GHG emissions` `of which non-reckonable` MINUS `of which excluded`

§§ `3 -- business facility`

-- s 3(1): "A business facility is a single site at which any business activity is carried out." (3): activities on more than one
-- parcel of land are at a single site "if the same person has operational control over the business activity, and -- (a) the
-- parcels of land are contiguous, adjacent or adjoining, or separated only by any road or pathway ..., or drain or waterway; or
-- (b) where paragraph (a) does not apply, there is a dependency between the activities ..., having regard to any circumstances
-- prescribed." The prescribed circumstances were not deposited; the dependency is a fact the operator states.
GIVEN `I control the activity on every parcel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parcels adjoin or are separated only by a road, path, drain or waterway` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activities on the parcels depend on each other` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my parcels one site` IF
        `I control the activity on every parcel`
    AND (   `the parcels adjoin or are separated only by a road, path, drain or waterway`
         OR `the activities on the parcels depend on each other`)

§§ `4 -- operational control`

-- s 4(1): a person has operational control "if the person has the authority to introduce and implement ... one or more of the
-- following: (a) operating policies; (b) health and safety policies; (c) environmental policies." (2): "Only one person can have
-- operational control over a business facility at any one time." (3): if more than one person satisfies (1), the person "that has
-- the greatest authority" is taken to have it.
GIVEN `I can introduce and implement operating policies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I can introduce and implement health and safety policies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I can introduce and implement environmental policies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `someone else has greater authority to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have operational control` IF
        (   `I can introduce and implement operating policies`
         OR `I can introduce and implement health and safety policies`
         OR `I can introduce and implement environmental policies`)
    AND NOT `someone else has greater authority to do so`

§§ `7(1)-(4) -- must I apply to register`

-- s 7(1): where the reckonable emissions of a business facility attain "the first emissions threshold (or higher) in any year
-- (called in this Part a trigger year)", the person in (1A) must apply "(a) to be registered as a registered person; (b) to
-- register the business facility as a reportable facility ...; and (c) if [they] also [attain] the second emissions threshold
-- (or higher) in the same trigger year, to register the business facility as a taxable facility". (1A): the person "having
-- operational control over the business facility on 31 December of the trigger year". (2): (1)(a) does not apply if "(a) the
-- person is already a registered person; or (b) the business facility will cease to be under the operational control of the
-- person by the time the person must make the application". (3), (4): (b) and (c) do not apply if already so registered.
GIVEN `my reckonable emissions in the year` IS A NUMBER
      `I had operational control on 31 December of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am already a registered person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the facility will leave my control before my application is due` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I apply to be registered as a registered person` IF
        `my reckonable emissions in the year` AT LEAST `the first emissions threshold`
    AND `I had operational control on 31 December of the year`
    AND NOT `I am already a registered person`
    AND NOT `the facility will leave my control before my application is due`

GIVEN `my reckonable emissions in the year` IS A NUMBER
      `I had operational control on 31 December of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the facility is already my reportable facility` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I apply to register the facility as a reportable facility` IF
        `my reckonable emissions in the year` AT LEAST `the first emissions threshold`
    AND `I had operational control on 31 December of the year`
    AND NOT `the facility is already my reportable facility`

GIVEN `my reckonable emissions in the year` IS A NUMBER
      `I had operational control on 31 December of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the facility is already my taxable facility` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I apply to register the facility as a taxable facility` IF
        `my reckonable emissions in the year` AT LEAST `the second emissions threshold`
    AND `I had operational control on 31 December of the year`
    AND NOT `the facility is already my taxable facility`

§§ `8(1)(a)(i) -- by when`

-- s 8(1)(a)(i): "where section 7(1) applies -- no later than 30 June of the year immediately after the trigger year".
GIVEN `the trigger year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I apply to register` IS Date 30 6 (`the trigger year` PLUS 1)

§§ `7(5), (6) and 8(1)(a)(ii) -- taking over a facility`

-- s 7(5): where X "(i) is a registered person of a business facility that is a reportable facility, or both ...; or (ii) is not a
-- registered person ... but had operational control over the business facility on 31 December of a trigger year" and "X
-- transfers operational control over the business facility to another person (Y), then Y must apply ... (c) to be registered as
-- a registered person; and (d) to register the business facility as a reportable facility or as both ... (as the case may be)".
-- (6): (5)(c) does not apply if Y is already a registered person.
GIVEN `the person I took over from was registered for the facility or controlled it on 31 December of a trigger year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I apply to register the facility after taking it over` IF
    `the person I took over from was registered for the facility or controlled it on 31 December of a trigger year`

GIVEN `the person I took over from was registered for the facility or controlled it on 31 December of a trigger year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am already a registered person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I apply to be registered as a registered person after taking over` IF
        `the person I took over from was registered for the facility or controlled it on 31 December of a trigger year`
    AND NOT `I am already a registered person`

-- s 8(1)(a)(ii): Y applies "(A) if, in the year immediately before the year of the transfer, the [reckonable emissions do] not
-- attain the second emissions threshold -- no later than 30 June of the year immediately after the year of the transfer; (B) if
-- -- (BA) at the time X transfers operational control to Y, the business facility is not registered as a taxable facility of X;
-- and (BB) in the year immediately before the year of the transfer, [they attain] the second emissions threshold (or higher),
-- no later than the later of ... (BC) 30 June of the year of the transfer; (BD) 30 days after the date of the transfer; and (C)
-- if, at the time X transfers operational control to Y, the business facility is registered as a taxable facility of X -- no
-- later than 30 days after the date of the transfer".
-- NOT COVERED: a facility that was X's taxable facility but whose emissions in the year before the transfer were below the
-- second threshold falls under both (A) and (C), which give different days, and the text does not say which prevails. The
-- answer is NOTHING rather than a guess.
GIVEN `the date of the transfer` IS A DATE
      `the facility was a taxable facility of the person I took over from` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its reckonable emissions in the year before the transfer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By when must I apply after taking over operational control` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facility was a taxable facility of the person I took over from` AND `limb A applies`
            THEN NOTHING
        IF `the facility was a taxable facility of the person I took over from`
            THEN JUST (`the date of the transfer` PLUS 30)
        IF `limb A applies`
            THEN JUST (Date 30 6 (DATE_YEAR `the date of the transfer` PLUS 1))
        OTHERWISE JUST (IF Day `30 June of the transfer year` AT LEAST Day `30 days after`
                        THEN `30 June of the transfer year`
                        ELSE `30 days after`)
    WHERE
        `limb A applies` MEANS `its reckonable emissions in the year before the transfer` LESS THAN `the second emissions threshold`
        `30 June of the transfer year` MEANS Date 30 6 (DATE_YEAR `the date of the transfer`)
        `30 days after` MEANS `the date of the transfer` PLUS 30

§§ `9(1)-(3) -- may I apply to deregister`

-- s 9(1) (taxable facility) and (3) (reportable facility): the registered person may apply to deregister if "(a) the registered
-- person ceases to have operational control over the business facility; (aa) the registered person has operational control ...
-- but has ceased to operate the business facility and has no intention of resuming its business activity within the next 36
-- months after such cessation; (b) the [reckonable emissions do] not attain the second [first] emissions threshold for each of 3
-- consecutive years; or (c) where any modification ... is completed and -- (i) [the emissions] in the year in which the
-- modification is completed ... [do] not attain the [threshold]; and (ii) [they are] unlikely to attain the [threshold] in each
-- of the 2 consecutive years immediately following." Whether they are unlikely to is a fact the operator states (the text does
-- not say who judges it; the Agency may refuse an incomplete application under s 10(2)).
DECLARE `Registration` IS ONE OF
    `a reportable facility`
    `a taxable facility`

GIVEN `the registration` IS A `Registration`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the threshold for deregistering as` IS
    CONSIDER `the registration`
    WHEN `a reportable facility` THEN `the first emissions threshold`
    WHEN `a taxable facility` THEN `the second emissions threshold`

GIVEN `the registration` IS A `Registration`
      `I have ceased to have operational control` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have stopped operating it with no intention of resuming within 36 months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `consecutive years below the threshold` IS A NUMBER
      `a modification was completed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my reckonable emissions in the year it was completed` IS A NUMBER
      `they are unlikely to attain the threshold in each of the next 2 years` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to deregister the facility as` IF
        `I have ceased to have operational control`
    OR  `I have stopped operating it with no intention of resuming within 36 months`
    OR  `consecutive years below the threshold` AT LEAST 3
    OR  (    `a modification was completed`
         AND `my reckonable emissions in the year it was completed` LESS THAN `the threshold for deregistering as` `the registration`
         AND `they are unlikely to attain the threshold in each of the next 2 years`)

-- s 9(2): "a registered person must give the Agency advance written notice of the date that the operational control ... is to
-- cease, at least 45 days before that date." Failing to, without reasonable excuse, is an offence (s 54(5)).
GIVEN `the day my control is to cease` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I give the Agency notice that my control will cease` IS Date (Day `the day my control is to cease` MINUS 45)

§§ `11, 12 -- emissions reports`

-- s 11(1): "Where a registered person has for any part of a year operational control over a business facility that is a
-- reportable facility of the registered person, the registered person must submit to the Agency for the Agency's approval, an
-- emissions report for that business facility for that year". (3): the obligation "arises at the end of the reporting period".
-- The day by which the report must be submitted is not in the Act.
GIVEN `the facility is my reportable facility` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I had operational control for any part of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I submit an emissions report for the year` IF
    `the facility is my reportable facility` AND `I had operational control for any part of the year`

-- s 12(1): where the facility "is a taxable facility of a registered person", the report must be prepared on a monitoring plan,
-- "be verified by an accredited external auditor" and be accompanied by the auditor's report. (2): verification is not needed
-- "insofar as it relates to any non-reckonable GHG emission". (3): nor for any period that falls "(a) before the approval of the
-- Agency under section 13 for the monitoring plan; or (b) after the deregistration of the business facility as a taxable facility".
GIVEN `the facility is my taxable facility` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part of the period is after my monitoring plan was approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part of the period is after deregistration as a taxable facility` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the emissions are non-reckonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must this part of my report be verified by an accredited external auditor` IF
        `the facility is my taxable facility`
    AND `the part of the period is after my monitoring plan was approved`
    AND NOT `the part of the period is after deregistration as a taxable facility`
    AND NOT `the emissions are non-reckonable`

§§ `Third Schedule -- the carbon tax rate and the carbon price`

-- Third Schedule Part 1: "(a) for carbon tax for GHG emissions in 2023 or any earlier emissions year -- $5/tCO2e; (b) ... in 2024
-- or 2025 -- $25/tCO2e; (c) ... in 2026 or any later emissions year -- $45/tCO2e."
GIVEN `the emissions year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the carbon tax rate for` IS
    BRANCH IF `the emissions year` AT MOST 2023 THEN 5
           IF `the emissions year` AT MOST 2025 THEN 25
           OTHERWISE                               45

-- Third Schedule Part 2: "Subject to section 31A, a fixed-price carbon credit has a value as follows: (a) ... purchased in 2024
-- or any earlier year -- $5; (b) ... purchased in 2025 or 2026 -- $25; (c) ... purchased in 2027 or any later year -- $45."
-- s 31A (conversion on a change in the carbon price) is not encoded.
GIVEN `the year of purchase` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the carbon price of a credit bought in` IS
    BRANCH IF `the year of purchase` AT MOST 2024 THEN 5
           IF `the year of purchase` AT MOST 2026 THEN 25
           OTHERWISE                               45

§§ `16, 20C -- the carbon tax`

-- One case: one facility for one emissions year, as the operator would describe it.
DECLARE `Facility year` HAS
    `emissions year` IS A NUMBER
    `it was my taxable facility in the year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `GHG emissions` IS A NUMBER
    `non-reckonable emissions` IS A NUMBER
    `excluded emissions` IS A NUMBER
    `allowance awarded to me for the year` IS A NUMBER
    `Division 1A applies to the year` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the year` IS A `Facility year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the reported reckonable emissions of` IS
    `my reckonable emissions as reported` (`the year`'s `GHG emissions`) (`the year`'s `non-reckonable emissions`) (`the year`'s `excluded emissions`)

-- s 16(1): "A tax, called the carbon tax, is charged on the total amount of reckonable GHG emissions in any year (called in this
-- Act an emissions year) of a business facility that is a taxable facility of any registered person in that year." (2): "Subsection
-- (1) does not apply if the total amount of the reckonable GHG emissions in that emissions year does not attain the second
-- emissions threshold." (4): the tax "accrues as a liability of the registered person having operational control over the
-- taxable facility at the end of the ... last reporting period for the emissions year".
GIVEN `the year` IS A `Facility year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I charged carbon tax for the year` IF
        `the year`'s `it was my taxable facility in the year`
    AND `the reported reckonable emissions of` `the year` AT LEAST `the second emissions threshold`

-- s 16(3): the tax is "A x B", A being the emissions "rounded up to the nearest metric tonne" and B the Third Schedule rate.
-- s 20C: where the facility "is eligible for any allowance for any emissions year", the tax is "(A - C) x B", C being the allowance
-- and "(A - C) ... rounded up to the nearest metric tonne". s 20B: Division 1A applies to emissions years from 1 January 2024 "up
-- to and including such date as the Minister may prescribe" -- not deposited, so whether it still applies is an input. The award
-- itself is the Minister's (ss 20D, 20E) and is an input.
-- NOT COVERED: an emissions year before 2024 (s 16 was rewritten by Act 37 of 2022 wef 1 January 2024 and the earlier text was not
-- deposited), and an allowance larger than the emissions (the text does not say what (A - C) below zero means).
GIVEN `the year` IS A `Facility year`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What carbon tax am I charged for the year` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the year`'s `emissions year` LESS THAN 2024 THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT `Am I charged carbon tax for the year` `the year` THEN JUST 0
        IF `an allowance counts` AND `the year`'s `allowance awarded to me for the year` GREATER THAN `A`
            THEN NOTHING
        IF `an allowance counts`
            THEN JUST (CEILING (`A` MINUS `the year`'s `allowance awarded to me for the year`) TIMES `B`)
        OTHERWISE JUST (`A` TIMES `B`)
    WHERE
        `A` MEANS CEILING (`the reported reckonable emissions of` `the year`)
        `B` MEANS `the carbon tax rate for` (`the year`'s `emissions year`)
        `an allowance counts` MEANS
                `the year`'s `allowance awarded to me for the year` GREATER THAN 0
            AND `the year`'s `Division 1A applies to the year`

§§ `17(1) -- by when must I pay`

-- s 17(1): the tax "must be paid -- (a) against an assessment pursuant to section 21(1) or (2), by the later of -- (i) 30 September
-- of the year immediately following the emissions year; or (ii) 30 days after the date of service on the registered person of the
-- notice of assessment; and (b) against any other assessment, within 30 days after the date of service". s 21(1) is the assessment
-- made on approving the verified report; s 21(2) the best-judgment assessment.
GIVEN `the assessment is under section 21(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the emissions year` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the notice of assessment was served on me` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I pay the tax` IS
    IF `the assessment is under section 21(1) or (2)` AND Day `30 September next` AT LEAST Day `30 days after service`
    THEN `30 September next`
    ELSE `30 days after service`
    WHERE
        `30 September next` MEANS Date 30 9 (`the emissions year` PLUS 1)
        `30 days after service` MEANS `the day the notice of assessment was served on me` PLUS 30

§§ `17(2), (3) -- how many credits`

-- s 17(2)(a): payment is "by the surrender of fixed-price carbon credits"; (3): "the number of fixed-price carbon credits that must
-- be surrendered ... is the number assessed by the Agency to have a total carbon price equal to the amount of tax charged."
-- NOT COVERED: s 17(3) does not say how a fractional number is rounded (s 17(3B) rounds down, but only for a revised assessment), so
-- a tax that is not a whole number of credits gives NOTHING. Surrender of international credits (s 17(3A), s 33B) is not encoded.
GIVEN `the tax` IS A NUMBER
      `the year I buy the credits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many fixed-price carbon credits must I surrender` IS
    IF `the number` EQUALS TRUNC `the number` 0
    THEN JUST `the number`
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the number` MEANS `the tax` DIVIDED BY `the carbon price of a credit bought in` `the year I buy the credits`

§§ `17(4) -- paying late`

-- s 17(4): if the tax is not paid in full in time, "(a) a financial penalty of 5% of the amount of tax assessed and remaining unpaid,
-- is payable in addition to the tax"; "(c) ... if the amount of tax remaining unpaid is not paid within 60 days after the imposition
-- of the financial penalty under paragraph (a), an additional financial penalty of 1% of the amount of tax remaining unpaid is payable
-- for each completed month that the tax remains unpaid, but not exceeding triple the amount of tax remaining unpaid in total."
-- READING: the cap is applied to the 1% penalties; the text leaves open whether "in total" also takes in the 5%, and from when the
-- completed months are counted, so the months are a fact the operator states. Relief or remission by the Agency or the Minister
-- (s 18) is a discretion and is not applied.
GIVEN `the tax remaining unpaid` IS A NUMBER
      `it was still unpaid 60 days after the 5% penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `completed months it has remained unpaid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What late-payment penalty can I be made to pay` IS
    `the 5% penalty` PLUS `the 1% penalties`
    WHERE
        `the 5% penalty` MEANS `the tax remaining unpaid` TIMES 0.05
        `the 1% penalties` MEANS
            IF `it was still unpaid 60 days after the 5% penalty`
            THEN min (`the tax remaining unpaid` TIMES 0.01 TIMES `completed months it has remained unpaid`) (`the tax remaining unpaid` TIMES 3)
            ELSE 0

-- s 17(4)(b): the Agency "must serve a demand note on the registered person and if payment is not made within 30 days after the date
-- of the service of the demand note, the Agency may proceed to enforce payment". Not paying the tax in a demand note is an offence
-- (s 59). The duty, from the day the demand note is served:
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF `me`
DECLARE `Act of mine` IS ONE OF `pay the tax and penalty in the demand note`

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act of mine`
DECIDE `my duty on being served a demand note` IS
    PARTY `me`
    MUST  `pay the tax and penalty in the demand note`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH

§§ `34(1), (2) -- appeal to the Minister`

-- s 34(1): a registered person "aggrieved by a decision of the Agency -- (a) refusing to deregister a business facility as a taxable
-- facility ...; (b) refusing to approve a verified emissions report or a monitoring plan ...; (c) refusing to refund any tax under
-- section 19(1) or credit any fixed-price carbon credit ... under section 19(2); or (d) refusing to revise any assessment ... pursuant
-- to section 23, may appeal against the decision to the Minister." (2): "within 30 days after the date of service of the Agency's
-- decision appealed against."
DECLARE `Decision of the Agency` IS ONE OF
    `refusing to deregister my taxable facility`
    `refusing to deregister my reportable facility`
    `refusing to approve my verified emissions report`
    `refusing to approve my monitoring plan`
    `refusing to refund tax or credit fixed-price carbon credits under section 19`
    `refusing to revise my assessment under section 23`
    `serving a demand note for the 5% late-payment penalty`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Decision of the Agency`
      `days since the decision was served on me` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I appeal to the Minister` IF
        `days since the decision was served on me` AT MOST 30
    AND CONSIDER `the decision`
        WHEN `refusing to deregister my reportable facility` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `serving a demand note for the 5% late-payment penalty` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `54-59, 62(1) -- what can I be fined`

-- Each maximum as the text sets it, for a natural person or a company alike. `the tax concerned` is, for s 54(3), "the tax for
-- which the person would have been liable had the business facility been registered as a taxable facility"; for s 56(2)-(5), "the
-- tax undercharged"; for s 59, "the amount of tax specified in the demand note as being outstanding". s 55(3), 56(6) and 57(3):
-- the inaccuracy offences do not apply "to any inaccuracy notified to the Agency under section 15(1)".
DECLARE `Offence` IS ONE OF
    `not applying to be registered, s 54(1)`
    `not applying to register a reportable facility, s 54(2)`
    `not applying to register a taxable facility, s 54(3)`
    `a false statement in a registration application, s 54(4)`
    `not giving 45 days notice that my control will cease, s 54(5)`
    `not submitting an unverified emissions report, s 55(1)`
    `an inaccurate unverified emissions report, s 55(2)(a)`
    `a second inaccurate unverified emissions report, s 55(2)(b)`
    `not submitting a verified emissions report, s 56(1)`
    `an inaccurate verified emissions report, s 56(2)`
    `an inaccurate verified emissions report through negligence, s 56(3)`
    `an inaccurate verified emissions report wilfully to evade tax, s 56(4)`
    `an inaccurate verified emissions report by fraud and wilfully to evade tax, s 56(5)`
    `not submitting a monitoring plan, s 57(1)`
    `an inaccurate monitoring plan, s 57(2)`
    `not notifying an error within 7 working days, s 58`
    `not paying the tax in a demand note, s 59`
    `not keeping records, s 62(1)`
    `a second records offence, s 62(1)`

DECLARE `Exposure` HAS
    `the most I can be fined` IS A NUMBER
    `further fine for each day the offence continues after conviction` IS A NUMBER
    `the most years I can be imprisoned` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`
      `the tax concerned` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Exposure`
DECIDE `What is the most I can be made to pay or serve for` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `not applying to be registered, s 54(1)` THEN `Exposure` OF 5000, 0, 0
    WHEN `not applying to register a reportable facility, s 54(2)` THEN `Exposure` OF 5000, 0, 0
    -- s 54(3): "(a) 10% of the tax ...; (b) an amount not exceeding $10,000, and to a further penalty of $50 for every day"
    WHEN `not applying to register a taxable facility, s 54(3)` THEN `Exposure` OF (`the tax concerned` TIMES 0.1 PLUS 10000), 50, 0
    -- s 54(4): "$5,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or ... both"
    WHEN `a false statement in a registration application, s 54(4)` THEN `Exposure` OF 5000, 0, 0.5
    WHEN `not giving 45 days notice that my control will cease, s 54(5)` THEN `Exposure` OF 10000, 0, 0
    WHEN `not submitting an unverified emissions report, s 55(1)` THEN `Exposure` OF 1000, 50, 0
    WHEN `an inaccurate unverified emissions report, s 55(2)(a)` THEN `Exposure` OF 10000, 0, 0
    WHEN `a second inaccurate unverified emissions report, s 55(2)(b)` THEN `Exposure` OF 20000, 0, 0
    WHEN `not submitting a verified emissions report, s 56(1)` THEN `Exposure` OF 1000, 50, 0
    -- s 56(2): "a fine that is equal to the tax undercharged" -- a fixed amount, not a maximum
    WHEN `an inaccurate verified emissions report, s 56(2)` THEN `Exposure` OF `the tax concerned`, 0, 0
    -- s 56(3): "double the tax undercharged" and "a further fine ... not exceeding $5,000 or ... imprisonment ... not exceeding 3 years"
    WHEN `an inaccurate verified emissions report through negligence, s 56(3)` THEN `Exposure` OF (`the tax concerned` TIMES 2 PLUS 5000), 0, 3
    WHEN `an inaccurate verified emissions report wilfully to evade tax, s 56(4)` THEN `Exposure` OF (`the tax concerned` TIMES 3 PLUS 10000), 0, 3
    WHEN `an inaccurate verified emissions report by fraud and wilfully to evade tax, s 56(5)` THEN `Exposure` OF (`the tax concerned` TIMES 4 PLUS 50000), 0, 5
    WHEN `not submitting a monitoring plan, s 57(1)` THEN `Exposure` OF 1000, 0, 0
    WHEN `an inaccurate monitoring plan, s 57(2)` THEN `Exposure` OF 50000, 0, 0
    WHEN `not notifying an error within 7 working days, s 58` THEN `Exposure` OF 5000, 0, 0
    -- s 59: "a fine that is triple the amount of tax specified in the demand note as being outstanding"
    WHEN `not paying the tax in a demand note, s 59` THEN `Exposure` OF (`the tax concerned` TIMES 3), 0, 0
    WHEN `not keeping records, s 62(1)` THEN `Exposure` OF 5000, 0, 0
    WHEN `a second records offence, s 62(1)` THEN `Exposure` OF 10000, 0, 3

-- s 55(3), 56(6), 57(3): an inaccuracy the operator notified under s 15(1) -- within "7 working days after the discovery" -- is
-- not an offence under s 55(2), 56(2)-(5) or 57(2).
GIVEN `I submitted an inaccurate report or plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I notified the Agency of the inaccuracy under section 15(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be convicted for the inaccuracy` IF
    `I submitted an inaccurate report or plan` AND NOT `I notified the Agency of the inaccuracy under section 15(1)`
